  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output A.1. More accurate and sustainable statistics on decent work using the latest statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">The National Bureau of Statistics of Seychelles strentghened the national labour market statistics by carrying out the School to work transition and the impacts of COVID surveys. Furthermore, the NBS used the ILO model questionnaire for Labour Force Survey which adheres to the 19th ICLS Resolution and 20th  ICLS Resolution. The ILO provided technical assistance to the NBS in the developement of questionnaires and methodologies to undertake the labour market surveys such as the school to work transition, the impacts of COVID and the Labour Force. Moreover, the ILO supported the participation of the NBS in the online Workshop on 20th ICLS Resolution on Work Relationship held from 1 to 2 June 2021.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">A.1.1. Number of member States that strengthen their labour market statistics, standards and information systems through improved statistical surveys and use of other statistical sources</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
